course: dictionary
lesson: 808
title: Beginning: the first part
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A beginning is the first part, or the start, of something. Read this: «There seemed to be no end to this wood, and no beginning, and no difference in it.» The wood has no first part you can point to, so it feels endless. Words like «at the start» and «in the beginning» point to the very first moment.
explain: Beginning can also be a verb form. Begin means start, and beginning is its -ing form: «It is beginning to rain» means the rain is starting now. Look for a helper word such as is, was or are just before it. That tells you beginning is working as part of a verb.
explain: Use the words around it to check. «The red stop sign ends all scripts; pressing the green flag again starts them from the beginning.» From the beginning means from the very first part, not from where they stopped. Swap in start: «starts them from the start» still makes sense, so beginning means start.
fact: A beginning is the first part or the start of something.
fact: «In the beginning» means at the very first moment, before anything else happened.
fact: Beginning can also be the -ing form of begin, as in «It is beginning to rain».
fact: «From beginning to end» means all the way through, from the first part to the last.
fact: A good check is to swap in start: if start fits the sentence, beginning means the first part.
exercise: A story has a beginning, a middle and an end. What is the beginning of a story? | *The first part, where it starts | A picture on the cover | The part where it finishes | The last page
exercise: «It is beginning to rain.» What does beginning mean here? | It is the first part of the rain | It has stopped raining | *It is starting to rain | It is raining very hard
exercise: «We read the book from beginning to end.» What does from beginning to end mean? | *All the way through | Just the middle part | Backwards, from the last page | Only the first page
test: «In the beginning, the wood seemed endless.» What does in the beginning mean? | In the middle of the night | At the very last moment | *At the very first moment | Under the trees
test: «The game starts again from the beginning when you press the green flag.» Where does the game start again? | In the middle of the level | Nowhere, it pauses | At the red stop sign | *At the very first part
exam: «The universe had a beginning, so light has not had time to reach us from the most distant stars.» What does beginning mean in this sentence? | An ending | *The start of something | A pause in time | A bright light
